 -courses\, legal writing and visits to firms and agencies\; junior year br
 ings a paid LSAT course and mentors\; Summer II is an application boot cam
 p and a paid legal internship. UVA picks 8 to 12 scholars a year.\nWhere a
 nd when: UVA Law\, Charlottesville\, Va. · two summers (Summer I: May 27
 –June 19\, 2027) with LSAT help in between\nWho: Current sophomores work
 ing toward a bachelor's degree\, with strong preference for first-generati
 on students and students with limited money\nPay: No tuition or fees. Summ
 er I covers travel\, room and board and a $3\,000 stipend\; junior year in
 cludes an LSAT course stipend\; the Summer II internship pays\nApply: Appl
 ication\, two short essays\, one to three letters and a transcript (unoffi
 cial is fine). Decisions by April 15\nOpens: Open now\n\nDetails: https://
 maljahmi.github.io/qc-polisci-pathways/programs.html#lp-uva-roadmap-schola
 rs\nOfficial website: https://www.law.virginia.edu/academics/program/roadm
 ap-scholars-initiative\nAlways confirm the date on the official website.
